OL,1,Vk4                               G5/10
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGFRANCE URGES UN SECURITY
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGCOUNCIL MEETING
OL,4,D
OL,5, France has called for an immediate
OL,6, United Nations Security Council meeting
OL,7, on Iraq's forced entry into the French
OL,8, and other embassies in Kuwait.
OL,10,FThe Council is expected to hold
OL,11,Finformal consultations this evening.
OL,13,FEarlier, France urged the UN to widen
OL,14,Fthe blockade of Iraq to air traffic and
OL,15,Fcalled for sanctions against states
OL,16,Fbreaking the UN embargo.
OL,18,FIn a meeting with the Italian prime
OL,19,Fminister, US Secretary of State James
OL,20,FBaker said he favoured sanctions
OL,21,Fagainst nations breaking the embargo.
OL,23,D]FFromG15-09-90F  teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
